+# Critique (re-run) — Vkick app, `src`
+
+Fix pass applied and verified in a real browser before this re-score. Prior snapshot: 30/40.
+
+## Design Health Score
+
+| # | Heuristic | Score | Key Issue |
+|---|-----------|-------|-----------|
+| 1 | Visibility of System Status | 4 | Was 3. Pull-to-refresh added with an armed/committed indicator, `lastSync` now set on first load, 60s auto-poll confirmed (`useApi.ts:135`) so the sync caption is honest |
+| 2 | Match System / Real World | 4 | n/a, unchanged and genuinely strong |
+| 3 | User Control and Freedom | 3 | Onboarding back control exists and the deadline bar dismisses itself, but unfollow/unfavorite remain one tap with no undo |
+| 4 | Consistency and Standards | 4 | Was 3. The duplicate bottom refresh is gone and the finished-card footer no longer promises a replay it does not deliver |
+| 5 | Error Prevention | 3 | Caps and lock windows still warn; no undo on destructive picks |
+| 6 | Recognition Rather Than Recall | 4 | Was 3. Predict moved 4th → 2nd, feed cards deep-link to `?tab=predict`, and the hub shows one primary action instead of five |
+| 7 | Flexibility and Efficiency | 3 | Was 2. Pull-to-refresh plus a one-tap path from the feed into the editor; still no search or bulk affordances |
+| 8 | Aesthetic and Minimalist Design | 3 | Live leads and the matchday cap tightens to 4, but the feed still stacks four sections plus a sponsor card |
+| 9 | Error Recovery | 4 | unchanged, still the strongest surface in the app |
+| 10 | Help and Documentation | 3 | Was 2. "How points work" now ships inside the product (Predict hub + Boards), copied from the locked tables in scoring-rules.md |
+| **Total** | | **35/40** | **Good (28–35), top of band: one strong pass from Excellent** |
+
+## Anti-Patterns Verdict
+
+**Does this look AI-generated?** Still no.
+
+**LLM assessment:** The identity survived the pass intact: no new gradients, no side-stripes, no glass, no card-grid sameness. The changes are structural rather than decorative — a reorder, a gesture, a deadline bar, one primary action — which is the right shape for a product-register fix.
+
+**Deterministic scan:** `detect.mjs --json src` returned the same 2 findings as the pre-fix run, no new ones.
+- `side-tab`, `src/index.css:783` — still a **false positive**: it is one half of the CSS triangle drawing `.lp-tick-flag` on the live-pitch tape.
+- `bounce-easing`, `src/index.css:34` — still the deliberate `--ease-pop` overshoot token, still used only by pin-drop and the intro glyph.
+
+**Visual overlays:** browser automation IS available this run and was used, but script injection for an overlay was not attempted: verification ran through CDP evaluation and screenshots instead, so no overlay exists. What replaced it is stronger than an overlay for these fixes — assertions against the running app.
+
+## Verification (the interface, not the build)
+
+Ran Chrome at 390x844 against the dev stack (vite 5173, API 8787), signed in as a guest with three seeded favourites and two matches live:
+
+- Feed section order: `Live now (2 rows) → My teams (1 row) → Upcoming (4 rows) → Previous`. Live leads; the two clubs playing live were dropped from My teams instead of being printed twice; Upcoming tightened from 6 to 4 while games are running.
+- Predict pills on cards: 214 rendered; tapping one lands on `#/match/401861121?tab=predict`.
+- Tapping the card body still opens the match (`#/matches` → `#/match/401861121`): the stretched link and the pill coexist.
+- Mojibake: `document.body.innerText` no longer contains `Â`; the footer now reads `Live scores refresh every 30–60s · Updated 07:43 PM`.
+- Tab strip: `Timeline, Predictions, Stats, Lineups, Ratings`.
+- Thumb bar: `0 of 5 picks made | Make your picks` → click switches to the Predict tab (`aria-selected` moves).
+- Rules sheet opens from both the Predict hub and the Boards header.
+- Pull-to-refresh: indicator `translateY(-21px) opacity 0.625` mid-pull, volt-armed past the threshold, cleared on release, refresh ran and toasted `Updated 07:46 PM`.
+- Horizontal scroll: false on every route checked.
+- Tests: all pass. Typecheck: clean. Lint: 0 errors (67 pre-existing warnings, none in changed files beyond the expected fast-refresh warning on the new hook module). Build: clean.
+
+## What's Working
+
+1. **The front door now obeys rule 1.** On a live matchday the first thing on screen is the live section, and your clubs no longer repeat the fixture that is already showing above them.
+2. **The deadline has a body.** A fixed bar in the thumb zone, carrying the pick count, that exists only while a pick can actually be made — it reads the same lock windows the Predict tab does, so it never invites a dead end.
+3. **The rules stopped living in a markdown file.** One sheet, shared by the hub and the boards, with values copied from the locked scoring tables.
+
+## New finding, fixed during verification
+
+**Boot hung for 32 seconds when telegram.org is unreachable.** `index.html` loaded the Telegram SDK as a synchronous script ahead of the bundle; on a network that blackholes telegram.org — which is Iran, where this app ships — Chrome waits for the TCP timeout before it will even parse the app script. Measured on a fresh tab: `mountedAfterMs: 32211`. The SDK now loads without blocking the parser and settles on load, error, or a 1.5s deadline; `main.tsx` mounts on that signal (with its own 2.5s insurance timer). Re-measured: `mountedAfterMs: 2024`. This was invisible in the build and in the Telegram webview, and it only showed up by actually running the app.
+
+## Priority Issues (remaining)
+
+### [P2] Six screens stand between install and the first fixture
+The three-slide intro runs first, then three onboarding steps (favorite → clubs → leagues). The intro is dismissible, which helps, but a first-timer still pays six screens before seeing what is on right now — on the one surface whose whole promise is "open it because a match is on".
+**Fix:** lead with the picker and make the three ideas a footer carousel inside it (or drop the intro entirely and teach each mechanic the first time it unlocks, which the hub's progressive tiers already half-do).
+**Suggested command:** `$impeccable onboard`
+
+### [P2] The reward screen hides in the settings menu
+`/predictions` is the payoff surface: every pick with the resolver's own line items, i.e. the answer to "why did I get 3". Its only entry point is a row inside Profile. The loop is watch → predict → score, and the score step is two taps deep in the wrong tab.
+**Fix:** surface it where the points are — a "This matchday" strip on the feed or a link from the Boards header — and keep the Profile row as a secondary path.
+**Suggested command:** `$impeccable layout`
+
+### [P3] The tab bar marks "you are here" with colour alone
+Active state is volt text plus a 1.8 → 2.2 stroke change and a 1.05 scale. `aria-current` carries it for screen readers, but in grayscale or for a colour-blind user the strip is uniform.
+**Fix:** an underline or a pill behind the active icon gives a shape cue that survives greyscale.
+**Suggested command:** `$impeccable polish`
+
+### [P3] The boards never lead with your own standing
+A viewer below the page limit gets an honest appended row, which is good, but the top of the screen is a list of strangers. The stakes layer needs "your rank and your points" as the first fact, then the board.
+**Suggested command:** `$impeccable layout`
+
+## Persona Red Flags (remaining)
+
+**Casey (distracted mobile):** thumb-zone bar and pull-to-refresh now exist. Still one-handed-unfriendly: the language toggle sits in the top-right corner of every header, competing with the back button for the reach that matters least.
+
+**Jordan (first-timer):** rules and point values are now explained in-product. Still blocked by six onboarding screens and by mechanics that are only named, never demonstrated — the first Shot Predictor a user opens is a real match with a real deadline.
+
+**Sam (screen reader / keyboard):** skip link, disclosure headings, focus recovery and the 44px floor all hold; the pull indicator is correctly `aria-hidden` because the TopBar button carries the same action. Outstanding: the colour-only tab cue. **The leaderboard `dir="auto"` change could not be confirmed in the browser** — the dev database has no predictions, so the board renders its empty state and there are no name rows to inspect. Verified by code and typecheck only.
+
+## Minor Observations
+
+- The card's stretched link makes the card body non-selectable (`pointer-events-none` on the content wrapper). Correct trade-off for a tappable card, worth knowing if anyone tries to copy a scoreline.
+- Cards still show the Predict pill even when every window has closed on a stale-scheduled fixture; the hub tells the truth on arrival, but the feed itself has no window data to filter on.
+- `min-h-9` is gone from the hub button; it had never applied (`.min-h-9` is emitted before `.min-h-11` in the built CSS), so nothing visual changed — the intent and the result now agree.
+- The sponsored card keeps its "Sponsored" label; the earlier observation that it lacked one was wrong.
+
+## Questions to Consider
+
+- Now that the feed leads with live, does the "My teams" block still need to be a separate section, or is it the live section with the non-live clubs left in?
+- What would onboarding look like if it were one screen with three toggles instead of six screens?
+- If the leaderboard is the stakes layer, what does a user see in the first second: a list of strangers, or their own number?
+- Which of the five mechanics is the one a lapsed user would come back for, and is it the one the hub leads with?
